  {
    "id": "anno-hitoyoshi_lower_p244_right-03",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "三大隊　内一隊士族準士族相混五十人小隊ニテ四小隊ヲ以大隊ニ組相用候　内二隊炮卒五十人一小隊ニテ六小隊ヲ以テ一大隊ニ組相用候"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "三大隊　内一隊は士族・準士族相混じ、五十人小隊にて四小隊を以て大隊に組み相用い候　内二隊は炮卒五十人一小隊にて、六小隊を以て一大隊に組み相用い候"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Three battalions. The double-column interlinear note explains the composition: one of the three battalions mixes shizoku and quasi-shizoku, at fifty men to a platoon and four platoons to a battalion (200 men); the other two are of artillery sotsu, at fifty men to a platoon and six platoons to a battalion (300 men each, 600 in all). The three battalions therefore come to 800 men. The project's MASTER row reverses the two clauses (two shizoku battalions of 200 plus one sotsu battalion of 300, giving 700); the page reads 内一隊士族… and 内二隊炮卒…, so the scan gives one shizoku battalion and two artillery battalions."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "平戸三大隊"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "source": "images/lower_p244_right.jpg",
      "selector": {
        "type": "FragmentSelector",
        "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/",
        "value": "xywh=pixel:1903,1102,127,2231"
      }
    }
  },
  {
